# DTF tier manifest: plugins-disabled  (artifact-keeper#4650, fixed by #4651; 1.11.2)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. The oracle recreates only the backend with
# a tier-local override layered on compose.base.yml: fixtures/plugins.default.yml
# (PLUGINS_ENABLED unset) or fixtures/plugins.off.yml (PLUGINS_ENABLED=false).
# Both pin the json-file log driver so the startup lines can be read with
# docker logs.
#
# THE FEATURE
# PLUGINS_ENABLED=false (config.rs parse_opt_out_flag; unset = on) makes
# initialize_wasm_plugins_if_enabled() return None before the registry, the
# Wasmtime engine, the core format-handler sync and the startup plugin load,
# logging `WASM plugin runtime disabled by operator`
# (event=plugins_disabled_by_operator), and routes.rs skips the /api/v1/plugins
# (user + admin), /api/v1/formats (user + admin) and /ext nests. Before #4651
# the variable did not exist: the runtime always started and the routes were
# always registered.
#
# THE GATES
#   (CONTROL)  both images, PLUGINS_ENABLED unset: the startup log has
#              "Initializing WASM plugin system" and "WASM plugin system
#              initialized"; GET /api/v1/plugins is 200 {items: [...]};
#              GET /api/v1/formats/maven is 200; POST
#              /api/v1/plugins/install/local {} is a 422 validation refusal
#              (the route exists); GET /ext/pdnope/<repo>/x is 404 "No protocol
#              handler for format 'pdnope'" (the WASM proxy answered).
#   (FIX)      PLUGINS_ENABLED=false: the same five routes plus
#              POST /api/v1/formats/maven/disable answer the router's 404 with
#              no plugin/handler body; the log has the
#              plugins_disabled_by_operator line and none of the runtime's
#              initialization / format sync / plugin load lines.
#              RED on 1.11.1: the flag is ignored, every route answers as in
#              the control and the runtime initializes.
#   (CONTROL)  both images, PLUGINS_ENABLED=false: a generic upload round-trips
#              byte-exact and is listed; unsetting
#              the flag again restores the routes.
#
# NOT GATED HERE: /api/v1/system/config has no plugin-runtime field (its
# plugin_signing block reports signature policy only, on 1.11.2 and on main),
# so there is nothing there to assert. No plugin is installed, so "stored
# plugins are not loaded at startup" is asserted through the absent load and
# init lines only.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: a few logins across three boots.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
